<title>UK: British-Borneo H1 pretax surges 45 pct.</title>
<headline>British-Borneo H1 pretax surges 45 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		13.75		  vs 11.48</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 3.0		    vs 2.67</p>
<p> Pretax		     10.86		  vs 7.51</p>
<p> Turnover		   26.95		  vs 20.47</p>
<p>NOTE - Chief executive of exploration firm British Borneo Petroleum Syndicate Plc Alan Gaynor said its approach &quot;continues to produce excellent financial results and has created the opportunities, in the North Sea and the Gulf of Mexico, which should deliver further significant growth for shareholders&quot;.  Operating result	 11.39		  vs 8.89</p>
<p> Interest paid	    0.53		   vs 1.38</p>
<p> Tax			  2.76		   vs 2.30</p>
<p> Net taxed		  8.10		   vs 5.21</p>
<p> Retained		   6.19		   vs 4.00</p>
<p> Pay date		   October 22</p>
<p>Div registration date  October 1  Ex-div date		September 23</p>
</text>
